WEBVTT

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.060
Why you!

00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:45.390
I did it!

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:51.610
I'm such a genius!

00:00:59.090 --> 00:01:00.790
It can't be!

00:01:01.650 --> 00:01:06.790
Oh, somebody help me!

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:25.340
koi ni naranai ne soba ni iru dake ja

00:01:18.240 --> 00:01:25.340
Just being close to you doesn't make love happen.

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:32.590
nazo wo kakete mo donkan na hito dakara

00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:32.590
Even if I make a puzzle you can't solve it because you're slow

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:39.750
natsu no fuku wo kite haru no umi ni kita

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:39.750
We came to the spring sea, wearing summer clothes.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:47.030
anata no SHATSU de yasashiku kabatte

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:47.030
Please cover me gently with your shirt.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.840
My heart iidasenai

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.840
My heart won't let me say

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.340
Please KISU shite tte

00:01:51.010 --> 00:01:54.340
"Please kiss me."

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:55.670
Day Dream

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:55.670
Day Dream...

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.000
yume wa fukurami

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:58.000
My dream gets bigger

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:04.150
sora ni takaku kieru

00:01:58.200 --> 00:02:04.150
and disappears high in the sky.

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:12.520
onna no ko wa dare datte shiawase ni nareru

00:02:05.090 --> 00:02:12.520
Any girl can be happy.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:19.330
koi ga hajimareba kagayakidasu

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:19.330
When they fall in love, they start shining.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:26.970
tatoe namida nagashite mo anata no sei nara

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:26.970
Even if the tears start flowing, or my heart aches,

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:34.410
mune wo itamete mo yashiku naru

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:34.410
if it's because of you, she'll become gentler

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:52.960
What am I supposed to do with all this, just by myself?

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.040
Morisato, you win!

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:03.120
Well, then, our rider for the college festival intercollegiate drag race is you,

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.870
Morisato Keiichi-kun!

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:07.800
Damn, me again?

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.880
Don't worry.

00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.430
We'll prepare a beauty for you!

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:18.650
And then they dump the whole thing on me!

00:03:18.650 --> 00:03:22.280
This is no machine, this is just parts!

00:03:27.230 --> 00:03:29.540
Oh, egg,

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:31.680
oh, egg,

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:34.040
I'm gonna mix you,

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.340
gonna mix you!

00:03:36.340 --> 00:03:38.850
You seem to be having fun!

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:42.050
I'm thinking about when it's done!

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.100
Let me try.

00:03:44.710 --> 00:03:47.250
OK, then I guess you can help me.

00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:49.850
Please mix the eggs till they're foamy.

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:51.970
I'll go make the cream.

00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:58.460
How will the cake taste like today?

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:03.660
One, two spoonfuls of sweets...

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:07.100
the taste of our love!

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:10.410
How can you do something as boring as this?

00:04:10.980 --> 00:04:12.470
Is that so?

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.910
I think cooking is a lot of fun!

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:18.750
Besides, as long as Keiichi-san likes it...

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:23.050
Urd?

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:25.720
I'll use my magic and...

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.220
I'm not cut out for menial labor.

00:04:36.220 --> 00:04:37.100
You can finish it up.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:43.070
I'm so bored!

00:04:43.530 --> 00:04:46.840
Hey, the engine mount's two millimeters off!

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:49.540
I may have to re-weld it!

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.810
Need some help?

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:52.870
It's OK.

00:04:52.870 --> 00:04:55.370
There's nothing you can help with, Urd.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.680
Don't give me that!

00:04:57.680 --> 00:05:00.290
To one such as I, this is nothing!

00:05:00.290 --> 00:05:04.340
Link hands, become a ring, and dance at the end of the

00:05:04.940 --> 00:05:07.490
hot exchange with the one designated!

00:05:05.510 --> 00:05:05.920
Stop it!

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:12.350
Kei-chan, I got your mesh hose.

00:05:13.190 --> 00:05:14.680
What're you doing, you two?

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:16.480
Sorry!

00:05:18.300 --> 00:05:21.820
I worked so hard to build this engine!

00:05:28.760 --> 00:05:31.030
I'm gonna go take a bath.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.160
Wait a minute, Kei-chan!

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:39.330
I'll just have to start over from scratch.

00:05:39.610 --> 00:05:41.130
That damn Urd!

00:05:41.130 --> 00:05:43.840
If only you hadn't messed it up!

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:58.060
Hello!

00:06:00.290 --> 00:06:02.280
Is anyone home?

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:11.360
Who are you?

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:13.190
What's, what's, what's going on?

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:13.370
What's, what's, what's going on?

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:14.860
What's, what's, what's going on?

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:15.460
Huh?

00:06:15.460 --> 00:06:16.200
Skuld!

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:19.370
What happened?

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:22.660
Onee-sama.

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:24.850
Long time no see!

00:06:24.850 --> 00:06:25.740
When did you get here?

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:27.110
Just now!

00:06:27.110 --> 00:06:30.050
Onee-sama, there's a strange man over there.

00:06:33.140 --> 00:06:35.480
Keiichi-san!

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:38.100
I'm sorry.

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:39.960
Don't worry about it.

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:41.940
I'm not angry, so please don't feel so bad.

00:06:43.090 --> 00:06:44.370
I'm Keiichi.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:46.130
That's my sister, Megumi.

00:06:46.130 --> 00:06:47.300
Nice to meet you.

00:06:47.300 --> 00:06:51.200
But I didn't know Belldandy had a sister as well!

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:53.070
Hey, where did you come from?

00:06:53.070 --> 00:06:54.950
I didn't see you walking in at all!

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:56.660
From the bathroom.

00:06:58.760 --> 00:07:00.640
Let's not worry about the details!

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:02.710
Tea is ready, everyone!

00:07:02.710 --> 00:07:04.180
It's finally done.

00:07:04.180 --> 00:07:06.670
Yay! It's a cake!

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.680
Here you go, Keiichi-san.

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:10.010
Thanks.

00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:12.590
Skuld, here you go.

00:07:12.590 --> 00:07:14.320
Did you apologize to Keiichi-san?

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:16.090
Yes, I did.

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:17.590
Why are you acting so stuck up?

00:07:17.590 --> 00:07:18.600
You shut up!

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.030
Well then.

00:07:20.030 --> 00:07:21.060
Let's dig in!

00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:31.070
So delicious!

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:33.610
This elegant taste and sweetness,

00:07:33.610 --> 00:07:40.650
it's not too strong and the tea's wonderful taste spreads all about in your mouth.

00:07:40.650 --> 00:07:42.320
Did you make this, onee-sama?

00:07:42.320 --> 00:07:43.640
Yes.

00:07:43.640 --> 00:07:46.880
It's my first attempt at making a cake from a local recipe.

00:07:46.880 --> 00:07:49.040
I hope you like it.

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:50.460
Yeah, it's great!

00:07:51.280 --> 00:07:54.470
I'm glad you like it!

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:56.060
Not at all!

00:07:56.060 --> 00:08:00.070
Everything you make is delicious!

00:08:00.070 --> 00:08:02.770
Keiichi-san, there's cream at the corner of your mouth!

00:08:02.770 --> 00:08:03.590
It's OK.

00:08:03.590 --> 00:08:05.070
I'll take care of it.

00:08:05.070 --> 00:08:06.050
But-

00:08:06.050 --> 00:08:08.180
not there, to the right.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:10.720
Your right, Keiichi-san.

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:12.190
There! You got it!

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:13.890
Hey you!

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:14.700
You disgust me!

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:20.390
In the first place, how dare you make onee-sama do this?

00:08:20.390 --> 00:08:21.970
She's...

00:08:21.970 --> 00:08:23.660
she's...

00:08:27.410 --> 00:08:29.360
Skuld!

00:08:30.320 --> 00:08:32.720
Well, I'm going back to work.

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:34.340
I'll leave the rest to you!

00:08:34.340 --> 00:08:35.470
I'm sorry about this...

00:08:36.480 --> 00:08:38.410
Kei-chan, wait!

00:08:38.410 --> 00:08:39.220
Thanks for the cake!

00:08:41.020 --> 00:08:43.110
What's wrong, Skuld?

00:08:43.110 --> 00:08:45.480
What are you so sad about?

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.920
Is there anything I can do?

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:50.000
Can I do something about your sadness?

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:52.120
Skuld!

00:09:04.840 --> 00:09:05.700
Skuld...

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:10.920
Onee-sama!

00:09:11.940 --> 00:09:13.890
Come home with me!

00:09:13.890 --> 00:09:16.810
You can't stay here!

00:09:16.810 --> 00:09:18.860
I can't!

00:09:18.860 --> 00:09:20.970
I have a contract with Keiichi-san.

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:25.850
The fact that a contract like that was accepted in the first place is weird!

00:09:25.850 --> 00:09:29.900
Why does onee-sama, a goddess, have to live with a human?

00:09:31.010 --> 00:09:33.830
Urd hasn't come home either,

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:38.330
and I have to deal with Bugs every day by myself and I...

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:40.000
I...

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:42.780
Ah, you're lonely. That's why you came here.

00:09:42.780 --> 00:09:44.740
I thought so!

00:09:44.740 --> 00:09:46.300
It's not like that!

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:49.480
Anyway, Urd, you've no right to talk like that!

00:09:49.480 --> 00:09:51.580
You can't even go back if you wanted to!

00:09:51.580 --> 00:09:55.340
That's why you'll always be a Second Class Goddess!

00:09:55.340 --> 00:09:56.720
Why you!

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.050
I won't take that from you!

00:09:58.050 --> 00:09:59.720
What? Wanna go for it?

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:01.470
Stop it!

00:10:02.910 --> 00:10:08.630
I'm sorry I made you lonely, Skuld.

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:09.910
But...

00:10:09.910 --> 00:10:14.340
I'm not here simply because of the contract.

00:10:14.340 --> 00:10:19.140
I simply must uphold this promise.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:24.410
As long as Keiichi-san wants me by his side I want to be there.

00:10:31.650 --> 00:10:32.920
Hey, Morisato-kun!

00:10:33.680 --> 00:10:35.070
You're working hard.

00:10:35.070 --> 00:10:36.590
Good! Good!

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:39.550
Wonderful!

00:10:39.550 --> 00:10:41.030
Beautiful!

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:42.530
That's our man! The pride of the Club!

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:45.100
You've got this much assembled already!

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:46.140
Well actually...

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:48.060
we brought you a nice present.

00:10:50.600 --> 00:10:51.770
What is this?

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:57.350
Well, it's something that'll double your engine power like magic.

00:10:57.350 --> 00:10:59.690
After all, there's no limit on engine displacement.

00:11:00.140 --> 00:11:02.280
It was hard to put together.

00:11:02.280 --> 00:11:06.910
Don't tell me you brought me a twin-engine.

00:11:07.120 --> 00:11:08.860
That's our Morisato!

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:09.490
Good guess!

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:11.930
What're you saying?

00:11:11.930 --> 00:11:14.930
The bike's more than half-built already!

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:18.300
Besides, a twin-engine is too heavy,

00:11:18.300 --> 00:11:19.500
and it makes the handling worse,

00:11:19.770 --> 00:11:21.740
and it won't improve the time as much as you'd expect.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:23.330
Morisato-kun!

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:24.980
We're heroes!

00:11:24.980 --> 00:11:27.740
Drag-racing heroes!

00:11:27.740 --> 00:11:32.100
A simple machine simply isn't our style, right?

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:37.190
If it increases our chances of winning by even 1%, we do it, right?

00:11:37.190 --> 00:11:40.820
That's the spirit of the Auto Club, right?

00:11:40.820 --> 00:11:41.990
What's that got to do with-

00:11:42.190 --> 00:11:42.950
Don't worry!

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:44.590
You can do it!

00:11:44.590 --> 00:11:47.660
You're the pride of our club!

00:11:47.660 --> 00:11:50.950
Are you guys still arguing about such basic things as engines?

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:52.620
Aoshima.

00:11:53.110 --> 00:11:54.120
You!

00:11:54.120 --> 00:12:00.640
At Nekomi Tech, we have an Auto Club and here you went and made a Racing Club!

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:03.750
If you call your child's play the Auto Club,

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:07.150
then we must be the Formula-1 team!

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:08.520
It's no contest!

00:12:08.520 --> 00:12:10.020
Say what?

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:11.720
What are you doing here anyway?

00:12:12.380 --> 00:12:13.990
Me?

00:12:14.600 --> 00:12:16.460
Isn't it obvious?

00:12:16.460 --> 00:12:20.440
I came to greet the lady who's going to be mine!

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:22.630
Hey, Tamiya-senpai.

00:12:22.630 --> 00:12:25.550
You haven't forgotten our deal, have you?

00:12:27.020 --> 00:12:27.990
Do we have a guest?

00:12:31.150 --> 00:12:33.830
Belldandy-san, you're as beautiful as ever!

00:12:34.440 --> 00:12:37.680
Your beauty is more precious than life,

00:12:37.680 --> 00:12:41.950
larger than the seven seas and brighter than the sun.

00:12:41.950 --> 00:12:44.520
If I could monopolize your beauty,

00:12:44.520 --> 00:12:49.010
I wouldn't mind being burned at the stake or sinking in the deep ocean.

00:12:49.830 --> 00:12:53.960
No matter what I might give you it would be meaningless before your beauty,

00:12:53.960 --> 00:12:57.060
but I want to present these roses,

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:00.310
so as to make you even more glamorous before my victory.

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:03.860
Thank you!

00:13:04.300 --> 00:13:05.740
W-Wait a minute!

00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:08.030
First you come barging in here, and now what do you think you're doing?

00:13:09.370 --> 00:13:10.570
Senpai...

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:16.000
you'd best figure out how to lose in style tomorrow.

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:18.250
Tamiya-senpai,

00:13:18.250 --> 00:13:20.660
don't forget our promise!

00:13:20.660 --> 00:13:24.380
In our club, the words "forget," "defeat," and "loss" don't exist.

00:13:25.960 --> 00:13:29.840
I won't let you withdraw prior to the race!

00:13:30.700 --> 00:13:34.310
Well, I'll see you at the racetrack tomorrow.

00:13:46.460 --> 00:13:47.450
Senpai,

00:13:47.450 --> 00:13:49.070
what's this promise?

00:13:49.490 --> 00:13:51.060
Well, Morisato-kun,

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:53.200
I'll leave the machine to you!

00:13:53.420 --> 00:13:54.450
Senpai!

00:13:56.940 --> 00:13:59.080
I guess I'll go back and watch TV.

00:13:59.570 --> 00:14:00.830
Kei-chan...

00:14:00.830 --> 00:14:04.600
if you're gonna use a twin-engine we've gotta make the strength calculations, and quick.

00:14:04.600 --> 00:14:07.590
After all, we can't rely on the main-frame they gave us!

00:14:14.950 --> 00:14:16.680
Twin-engine.

00:14:20.610 --> 00:14:21.930
What is this?

00:14:21.930 --> 00:14:24.420
It won't withstand the power in this shape!

00:14:24.420 --> 00:14:26.090
Here! And here!

00:14:26.090 --> 00:14:30.360
The calculations are all messed up, and I can't make sense of it.

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:32.660
This sucks! I can't leave such an ugly blueprint as it is!

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:38.870
Put a sub-frame within the main-frame here then it should be able to withstand the doubled power.

00:14:43.770 --> 00:14:45.510
It's finished!

00:14:48.270 --> 00:14:52.260
What beautiful equations!

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:58.450
Thanks, Skuld!

00:14:58.450 --> 00:15:00.860
You got a great sister!

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:02.290
You think so?

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:05.230
Thanks, Belldandy!

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:07.230
Oh, Keiichi-san!

00:15:11.440 --> 00:15:14.000
I hate you!

00:15:16.280 --> 00:15:17.660
I'm sorry about her, Keiichi-san.

00:15:18.010 --> 00:15:18.770
Awesome!

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:19.900
No problem!

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:21.940
She's saved us.

00:15:21.940 --> 00:15:24.250
Now that we have this, we can start assembly immediately!

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.150
She wasn't trying to be mean, either.

00:15:27.150 --> 00:15:29.880
Well, she's a kid-

00:15:30.390 --> 00:15:33.190
I'm not a kid!

00:15:35.070 --> 00:15:36.460
I'm sorry.

00:15:36.460 --> 00:15:37.350
It's OK, it's OK.

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:41.310
Well, shall we begin?

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:43.450
Oh, Skuld.

00:16:44.110 --> 00:16:45.640
Your blueprint saved us.

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:45.910
Thanks.

00:16:48.610 --> 00:16:51.770
How do you feel about onee-sama?

00:16:51.770 --> 00:16:54.770
Why did you make such an agreement?

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:55.920
Why?

00:16:55.920 --> 00:17:00.680
When she suddenly appeared and said "What do you wish for?"

00:17:00.680 --> 00:17:02.810
I thought it was a joke, and...

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:11.090
But if she does stay by my side forever oh, how happy we'll be!

00:17:11.090 --> 00:17:18.360
Ever since she came every day has been so full of happiness that I've forgotten all my troubles.

00:17:18.360 --> 00:17:22.600
She even makes me feel like I've known her...

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:23.950
since childhood!

00:17:24.760 --> 00:17:28.700
I don't know how long we can stay like this.

00:17:28.700 --> 00:17:30.520
But Megumi is here,

00:17:30.520 --> 00:17:32.040
Urd's here,

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:34.470
and now you've come.

00:17:35.440 --> 00:17:40.130
We've had some troubles but I can change them all into fond memories

00:17:40.650 --> 00:17:45.330
Because Belldandy is with me, I think.

00:17:45.990 --> 00:17:49.300
So I'm happy that I made that wish.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:52.190
So what?

00:17:52.190 --> 00:17:53.900
So what?

00:18:12.100 --> 00:18:12.810
All right!

00:18:12.810 --> 00:18:14.040
Well done, Morisato!

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:17.850
You can count on me!

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:20.820
This is honey lemon tea.

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:22.520
Please have some.

00:18:22.520 --> 00:18:23.290
Thanks!

00:18:23.290 --> 00:18:25.510
Oh, so you did it!

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.310
I've changed my opinion of you slightly.

00:18:30.830 --> 00:18:33.900
I see. Two GSX units.

00:18:33.900 --> 00:18:35.770
Even fuel injection!

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:40.290
But even so, this overnight job can't beat us.

00:18:40.290 --> 00:18:42.210
There's no comparison.

00:18:42.210 --> 00:18:43.980
Of course, we won't go easy on you, but-

00:18:43.980 --> 00:18:45.650
Wh-What?

00:18:45.650 --> 00:18:48.380
It's clear who'll be the winner.

00:18:48.380 --> 00:18:49.620
Belldandy-san...

00:18:49.620 --> 00:18:52.040
when the race is over, I'll be waiting for you in our clubroom.

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:55.390
Oh, don't tell me!

00:18:55.390 --> 00:19:00.630
Have you not heard from Tamiya-sempai, that if the Auto Club loses to our club,

00:19:00.630 --> 00:19:03.860
you'll become a member of our club?

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:04.470
What?

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:07.270
I haven't heard about that!

00:19:07.270 --> 00:19:07.560
Senpai!

00:19:10.010 --> 00:19:15.110
A-Anyway, without the consent of the person being bet on a deal as such is not acceptable!

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:16.560
It's OK.

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:22.480
We must keep promises no matter what.

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:24.450
But we won't lose this race!

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:26.950
Belldandy.

00:19:27.740 --> 00:19:31.890
So Belldandy's acceptance seals the deal.

00:19:31.890 --> 00:19:34.300
If you lose, you can't go back on your word!

00:19:34.300 --> 00:19:34.920
See ya!

00:19:38.440 --> 00:19:41.260
If Keiichi loses...

00:19:42.470 --> 00:19:44.370
Damn!

00:19:44.490 --> 00:19:46.170
I'm sorry, Belldandy,

00:19:46.170 --> 00:19:51.600
but I'm not worthy of you so I'll cancel the contract.

00:19:53.320 --> 00:19:55.320
I was wrong.

00:19:55.320 --> 00:19:57.490
Let's go home together.

00:19:59.060 --> 00:20:03.720
If that happens, onee-sama can go back to the Heavens and everyone will be happy.

00:20:03.720 --> 00:20:06.740
Which means...

00:20:09.560 --> 00:20:15.000
Well, it's finally the start of the Fourth Intercollegiate Golden Hammer drag race.

00:20:15.000 --> 00:20:16.920
First, we have the Ichinohashi Rocket Starters

00:20:17.400 --> 00:20:19.880
vs. the Iwashimizu Black Marks!

00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:31.510
The times we just got for the first race are Ichinohashi University: 7:856.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:33.690
The times we just got for the first race are Ichinohashi University: 7:856.

00:20:33.690 --> 00:20:35.940
Iwashimizu University: 8:042.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:39.990
Ichinohashi goes to the semi-finals!

00:20:39.990 --> 00:20:41.330
An impressive time.

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:43.860
Let's look forward to their performance in the semi-finals.

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:47.640
The second race is between Ushikubo University and the Nekomi Tech Auto Club.

00:20:47.640 --> 00:20:53.210
Oddly enough, Nekomi Tech has two teams participating but this is the original club.

00:20:52.310 --> 00:20:53.940
Go for it, OK,

00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:56.910
The same university has both an Auto Club and a Racing Club

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.630
Keiichi-san!

00:20:57.110 --> 00:20:59.880
and there are rumors that they are competing against one another.

00:21:07.670 --> 00:21:10.140
All right!

00:21:10.140 --> 00:21:11.070
They did it!

00:21:11.070 --> 00:21:13.560
Nekomi Tech showed the fighting spirit of the locals.

00:21:13.560 --> 00:21:17.770
There were some mistakes by their opponent but they've made the semi-finals!

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:17.770
Enjoy it while you can!

00:21:17.770 --> 00:21:20.810
Will we see a showdown with the Aoshima Racing Club?

00:21:18.200 --> 00:21:19.700
Thanks! Thank you!

00:21:19.700 --> 00:21:20.810
Thanks!

00:21:23.250 --> 00:21:28.980
Senpai, at around 6000 rpm it starts acting up and the vibrations throughout the frame are just awful!

00:21:28.980 --> 00:21:31.980
If we don't do something, we'll be in trouble in the semi-finals!

00:21:31.980 --> 00:21:33.400
OK, I hear you.

00:21:33.400 --> 00:21:35.480
Hey, Tam-chan, let's change the ROM!

00:21:35.480 --> 00:21:36.620
Sure.

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:39.710
Hey, you guys bring the rubber bearings!

00:21:40.060 --> 00:21:42.220
An unthinkable time has just been logged.

00:21:42.220 --> 00:21:46.930
Nekomi Tech's irregular team the Aoshima Racing Club, did a 7:036!

00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:48.660
It's the best time so far!

00:21:47.670 --> 00:21:49.560
Hey! What's going on?

00:21:48.660 --> 00:21:50.640
It feels as if these guys are out of our league!

00:21:49.560 --> 00:21:50.640
It's not good.

00:21:50.830 --> 00:21:53.960
What can they be doing?

00:21:51.370 --> 00:21:52.520
Good. Good.

00:21:52.520 --> 00:21:53.970
That's the way!

00:21:53.970 --> 00:21:58.600
Now if onee-sama will just notice that Keiichi is a jerk!

00:21:59.050 --> 00:22:00.430
All right!

00:22:00.430 --> 00:22:03.180
Ootaki and I will work on the electronics.

00:22:03.180 --> 00:22:06.680
The rest of you put rubber bearings in the engine mount!

00:22:06.680 --> 00:22:07.280
All right!

00:22:07.920 --> 00:22:10.430
Well, it'll be an easy victory for us.

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:14.450
But we sure went a lot faster than we did during testing!

00:22:43.620 --> 00:22:46.410
All right! That's our Morisato-kun!

00:22:46.410 --> 00:22:48.360
You've breezed into the finals!

00:22:48.770 --> 00:22:52.740
Keep it up and we'll beat Aoshima handily!

00:22:53.310 --> 00:22:54.930
Don't kid around like that!

00:22:54.930 --> 00:22:57.370
Those unusual vibrations haven't stopped yet!

00:22:58.010 --> 00:23:03.240
Then the problem's with the frame layout itself.

00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:05.910
All we can do is put a balancer in the handlebars.

00:23:05.910 --> 00:23:07.910
Better than nothing!

00:23:07.910 --> 00:23:10.840
You guys can win only if we make a mistake.

00:23:11.080 --> 00:23:16.150
But our driver holds the Japan drag-racing record,

00:23:16.150 --> 00:23:17.890
so we won't mess up.

00:23:17.890 --> 00:23:20.390
Why don't you just give Belldandy to us now,

00:23:20.390 --> 00:23:24.090
leave and spare yourselves the embarrassment?

00:23:24.090 --> 00:23:25.230
Never!

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:28.940
We will win!

00:23:29.790 --> 00:23:34.530
The goddess of victory does not smile on one such as you, who thinks only of winning.

00:23:35.200 --> 00:23:39.490
That's because the goddess of victory smiles on those who already have burning hearts!

00:23:40.210 --> 00:23:41.610
Very well.

00:23:41.610 --> 00:23:45.010
If you say so, then we'll let the outcome of the race decide.

00:23:45.010 --> 00:23:47.720
The margin of victory will be wide...

00:23:47.720 --> 00:23:50.690
and you'll change your mind.

00:23:50.690 --> 00:23:50.960
Until then.

00:23:52.730 --> 00:23:53.620
Belldandy,

00:23:53.620 --> 00:23:55.190
if I lose!

00:23:55.190 --> 00:23:56.530
It's OK.

00:23:56.530 --> 00:24:00.930
As long as you have a burning desire to win in your heart

00:24:01.850 --> 00:24:03.230
I believe the star of luck will be ascendant.

00:24:03.820 --> 00:24:05.140
Your right.

00:24:05.140 --> 00:24:08.230
Come to think of it, I do have strong allies!

00:24:08.730 --> 00:24:09.480
Urd,

00:24:10.170 --> 00:24:10.940
Belldandy,

00:24:11.140 --> 00:24:12.900
and now Skuld.

00:24:13.610 --> 00:24:17.110
I have three goddesses on my side, so how can I lose?

00:24:17.720 --> 00:24:19.580
It's the last race, so I'm going to go flat out.

00:24:20.590 --> 00:24:23.050
Well, the finals are exactly as we expected.

00:24:23.050 --> 00:24:25.780
Aoshima Formula Team vs. the Burning Gutsy Guys.

00:24:25.790 --> 00:24:28.220
Nekomi Tech's Auto Club vs. its Racing Club.

00:24:28.220 --> 00:24:29.690
It had to happen!

00:24:29.280 --> 00:24:30.880
Keiichi-san...

00:24:29.690 --> 00:24:32.890
What an interesting situation, almost as if it was fated!

00:24:31.480 --> 00:24:33.130
Wh-What?

00:24:32.890 --> 00:24:35.260
Who will the goddess of victory smile on?

00:24:33.130 --> 00:24:35.260
You forgot something!

00:24:41.250 --> 00:24:45.100
They're really putting on a show for us!

00:24:41.760 --> 00:24:43.710
For luck.

00:24:43.710 --> 00:24:45.690
I guarantee its effectiveness.

00:24:45.100 --> 00:24:46.440
Show-offs!

00:24:46.440 --> 00:24:49.560
Having come this far, you can't lose.

00:24:49.270 --> 00:24:51.330
A good-luck charm, huh?

00:24:49.560 --> 00:24:51.330
Go, Morisato-kun!

00:24:51.330 --> 00:24:53.790
I'm on your side too!

00:24:52.950 --> 00:24:53.790
OK!

00:25:14.510 --> 00:25:16.220
Damn!

00:25:25.400 --> 00:25:27.180
He did it!

00:25:27.900 --> 00:25:29.100
They did it!

00:25:29.100 --> 00:25:31.020
Nekomi Tech's Auto Club wins!

00:25:31.510 --> 00:25:33.070
The original team showed us their fighting spirit!

00:25:33.070 --> 00:25:37.080
Probably from trying so hard up till now, the Aoshima Formula team blew their engine

00:25:37.080 --> 00:25:38.990
and were thus defeated.

00:25:38.990 --> 00:25:41.490
They were strong at the beginning, so it's unfortunate,

00:25:41.490 --> 00:25:46.730
but as they are a recently formed team, they probably couldn't get their act together.

00:25:58.900 --> 00:26:01.000
We were perfect!

00:26:01.670 --> 00:26:04.070
Burning hearts?

00:26:16.790 --> 00:26:17.790
Oh my!

00:26:17.790 --> 00:26:19.130
How beautiful!

00:26:19.130 --> 00:26:20.330
You want it?

00:26:20.330 --> 00:26:21.090
Well...

00:26:21.090 --> 00:26:21.900
Really...?

00:26:21.900 --> 00:26:22.780
Just a minute.

00:26:25.510 --> 00:26:28.910
Damn, my money's all in my jacket!

00:26:28.910 --> 00:26:31.220
Who's fault is that!

00:26:31.220 --> 00:26:34.750
Can't you even buy a girl a present?

00:26:34.750 --> 00:26:36.520
Oh, that's all right!

00:26:36.520 --> 00:26:37.590
Sorry, Belldandy!

00:26:38.080 --> 00:26:39.630
What is this?

00:26:39.630 --> 00:26:43.170
You can't even do a little thing like that?

00:26:49.080 --> 00:26:51.880
I really <i>do</i> hate you!

00:27:06.070 --> 00:27:11.500
ude wo kunda hishochi no sanpo de

00:27:06.070 --> 00:27:11.500
Taking a stroll at a summer resort, arm in arm,

00:27:11.570 --> 00:27:17.010
guuzen deau CHAPERU no wedding

00:27:11.570 --> 00:27:17.010
we happened to come across a wedding at a chapel.

00:27:17.080 --> 00:27:22.480
asa no kaze ni tokekomu sanbika

00:27:17.080 --> 00:27:22.480
Gospels melting in the morning breeze...

00:27:22.550 --> 00:27:27.420
shiawase sou na futari

00:27:22.550 --> 00:27:27.420
A happy looking couple...

00:27:27.890 --> 00:27:30.450
omedetou! omedetou

00:27:27.890 --> 00:27:30.290
"Congratulations!"

00:27:30.360 --> 00:27:33.190
"Thank you!"

00:27:30.500 --> 00:27:33.190
arigatou! arigatou

00:27:33.260 --> 00:27:38.940
shiroi BU-KE wo sashidasu shinpu

00:27:33.260 --> 00:27:38.890
The bride tosses her white bouquet.

00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:45.530
shiawase shiawase 
 wakete ageru

00:27:38.960 --> 00:27:45.530
I will share my happiness with you.

00:27:45.600 --> 00:27:50.470
tonari de hohoemu kare

00:27:45.600 --> 00:27:50.470
The groom smiling next to her.

00:27:50.540 --> 00:27:55.740
futari noseta kuruma ga ugoku to

00:27:50.540 --> 00:27:55.740
When the car carrying the couple starts to move,

00:27:55.810 --> 00:28:01.380
anata ooki na akubi hitotsu

00:27:55.810 --> 00:28:01.380
you let out a big yawn.

00:28:01.450 --> 00:28:06.860
GYUTto ude wo tsunette ageta no

00:28:01.450 --> 00:28:06.860
I pinch your arm...

00:28:06.930 --> 00:28:13.090
omoi ni kidzuku kashira

00:28:06.930 --> 00:28:13.090
I wonder if you even realize how I feel?

00:28:24.860 --> 00:28:26.820
I obey destiny.

00:28:27.100 --> 00:28:29.610
She distinctly said that in his dream.

00:28:29.690 --> 00:28:32.460
From that moment, their time began to disintegrate...

00:28:32.540 --> 00:28:34.460
accelerating, getting louder.

00:28:34.540 --> 00:28:37.010
Onee-sama, don't look so sad.

00:28:37.090 --> 00:28:38.380
I'm sad too!

00:28:38.460 --> 00:28:41.860
After all, I finally got here only to
 have the next episode be the end!

00:28:41.940 --> 00:28:44.240
Hey, don't ruin the mood!
